# SECRETS. Read the CLI's own ignore list before trusting this file to
# be redundant: vercel's built-in upload ignores are
#
#   .hg .git .gitmodules .svn .cache .next .now .vercel .npmignore
#   .dockerignore .gitignore .*.swp .DS_Store .wafpicke-* .lock-wscript
#   .env.local .env.*.local .venv .yarn/cache .pnp* npm-debug.log
#   config.gypi node_modules __pycache__ venv CVS
#
# It ignores `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`. It does NOT ignore a plain
# `.env`, and `.gitignore` is in that list — so being gitignored buys
# nothing here: the file is neither uploaded nor read for ignore rules.
#
# This project's file is a plain `.env` holding live Firebase
# credentials, so until this line existed it was uploaded with every
# deployment and read by Vite at build time. Not a preview-only problem.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vercel uploads the working directory, and it is not reading .gitignore
# on this project's deploy path: the two source cookbooks are 298MB and
# 139MB, each over the 100MB per-file limit, and the deploy failed on
# them. Nothing here is needed to build the app.

# 437MB of cookbooks. Read only by the extraction step, never by the app
# — nothing in src/, index.html or vercel.json references them.
source-pdfs/

# The catalog pipeline. Runs on a laptop, not on a build server; the
# result it produces is committed at src/data/groceryCatalog.json.
tools/

node_modules/
